  "wire": [
    {
      "evidenceId": "E1",
      "quote": "Equation: ∆ = F θ (γ(sg(x)), γ(t) + X (i)) , X (i) = N(0, 1) • β • ∆t • (1 − i/τ ) ,(6)",
      "source": "P1",
      "resultRoleHintOnly": "unspecified",
      "tableDataOmitted": false
    },
    {
      "evidenceId": "E2",
      "quote": "For training, we conducted training for a total of 40k iterations.",
      "source": "P1",
      "resultRoleHintOnly": "unspecified",
      "tableDataOmitted": false
    },
    {
      "evidenceId": "E3",
      "quote": "During the initial 3k iterations, we solely trained the 3D Gaussians to attain relatively stable positions and shapes.",
      "source": "P1",
      "resultRoleHintOnly": "unspecified",
      "tableDataOmitted": false
    },
    {
      "evidenceId": "E4",
      "quote": "It can enhance the model's temporal generalization in the early stages of training, as well as prevent excessive smoothing in the later stages, thus preserving the details of objects in dynamic scenes.",
      "source": "P1",
      "resultRoleHintOnly": "unspecified",
      "tableDataOmitted": false
    },
    {
      "evidenceId": "E5",
      "quote": "A cardinal challenge in rendering these dynamic scenes lies in the encoding and effective utilization of temporal information, especially when addressing the reconstruction of monocular dynamic scenes, a task inherently involves sparse reconstruction from a single viewpoint.",
      "source": "P1",
      "resultRoleHintOnly": "unspecified",
      "tableDataOmitted": false
    },
    {
      "evidenceId": "E6",
      "quote": "One class of dynamic NeRF approaches models scene deformation by adding time t as an additional input to the radiance field.",
      "source": "P1",
      "resultRoleHintOnly": "unspecified",
      "tableDataOmitted": false
    },
    {
      "evidenceId": "E7",
      "quote": "However, this strategy couples the positional variations induced by temporal changes with the radiance field, lacking the geometric prior information regarding the influence of time on the scene.",
      "source": "P1",
      "resultRoleHintOnly": "unspecified",
      "tableDataOmitted": false
    },
    {
      "evidenceId": "E8",
      "quote": "However, for the task involving interpolated time, this kind of inconsistent scene at different times can lead to irregular rendering jitters.",
      "source": "P1",
      "resultRoleHintOnly": "unspecified",
      "tableDataOmitted": false
    },
    {
      "evidenceId": "E9",
      "quote": "To address this issue, we propose a novel annealing smooth training (AST) mechanism specifically designed for real-world monocular dynamic scenes:",
      "source": "P1",
      "resultRoleHintOnly": "unspecified",
      "tableDataOmitted": false
    },
    {
      "evidenceId": "E10",
      "quote": "where X (i) represents the linearly decaying Gaussian noise at the i-th training iteration, N(0, 1) denotes the standard Gaussian distribution, β is an empirically determined scaling factor with a value of 0.1, ∆t represents the mean time interval, and τ is the threshold iteration for annealing smooth training (empirically set to 20k).",
      "source": "P1",
      "resultRoleHintOnly": "unspecified",
      "tableDataOmitted": false
    },
    {
      "evidenceId": "E11",
      "quote": "Compared to the smooth loss introduced by methods of[34,38], our approach does not incur additional computational overhead.",
      "source": "P1",
      "resultRoleHintOnly": "profiling",
      "tableDataOmitted": false
    },
    {
      "evidenceId": "E14",
      "quote": "Subsequently, we jointly train the 3D Gaussians and the deformation field.",
      "source": "P1",
      "resultRoleHintOnly": "unspecified",
      "tableDataOmitted": false
    }
  ],
